## Who each plan suits

cards

### Basic

Lowest premium at $168 a year. No orthodontia, and the lowest annual maximum of $1,000.

### Plus

$336 a year with an annual maximum of $1,500. No orthodontia.

### Premier

$492 a year, with a $2,500 annual maximum and orthodontia at 50% up to $1,500 over a lifetime.

### Family Max

$756 a year, with a $3,000 annual maximum, no deductible and orthodontia at 50% up to $2,000. Pays off for families with ongoing orthodontia.

## Recommendation

We recommend **Premier** as the default plan. Family Max costs $264 more a year and only pays off for families with ongoing orthodontia.
